# Filesystems ({{ title }})

{{ title }} mounts several filesystems, each with a different purpose, technology, and
durability. Put data in the right place, and never assume a path is durable without
checking.

## Home — `/home/$USER` (`$HOME`)

- **Technology:** {{ filesystems.home.tech }}, with {{ filesystems.home.snapshots }}.
- **Use for:** source code, scripts, configuration, small files. It is
  medium-performance and space-limited.
- **Do NOT** stage large datasets or run heavy parallel job I/O here.

## Scratch — {% if scratch_path %}`{{ scratch_path }}/$USER` (`${{ env.scratch }}`){% else %}`${{ env.scratch }}`{% endif +%}

- **Technology:** {% if filesystems.scratch.tech %}{{ filesystems.scratch.tech }}, a high-performance parallel filesystem{% else %}a high-performance, large-capacity parallel filesystem{% endif %}.
- **Use for:** active job input/output and large working data. Point writable working
  files here (`${{ env.scratch }}`), not at home.{% if commands.findscratch %} Find the path with `{{ commands.findscratch }}`.{% endif +%}
{% if filesystems.scratch.purge_text is defined %}
- {{ filesystems.scratch.purge_text }}
{% elif filesystems.scratch.purge_days %}
- **Not backed up, and purged after {{ filesystems.scratch.purge_days }} days of inactivity** (by last access and
  content-modification time; touching metadata does not protect a file).
{% else %}
- **Not backed up, and purged after a period of inactivity.** The user guide does not state
  the window; check it before relying on scratch.
{% endif %}
{% if filesystems.depot or filesystems.fortress %}
- **Do NOT** treat scratch as durable storage — move anything you want to keep to {% if filesystems.depot and filesystems.fortress %}Data
  Depot or Fortress{% elif filesystems.depot %}Data Depot{% else %}Fortress{% endif %}.
{% else %}
- **Do NOT** treat scratch as durable storage — move anything you want to keep to
